# Implementation Plan — Phase 3: Real Data Integration & Complete DB Connection

Establish **MongoDB as the single source of truth for 100% of persistent business data** across the FastAPI backend, React Admin Web Portal, and React Native / Expo Mobile Alumni Application.

Phase 3 guarantees that every displayed business value (alumni, batches, events, attendance counts, announcements, memories, and dashboard metrics) is dynamically queried from MongoDB, and every user/admin action persists to MongoDB with zero mock business data in production paths.

---

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Single Source of Truth Architecture**:
> - All persistent business data originates from MongoDB collections (`schools`, `users`, `alumni`, `batches`, `events`, `event_attendance`, `checkins`, `announcements`, `memories`, `notifications`, `audit_logs`).
> - Frontend state in React and React Native is strictly scoped to transient UI state (loading spinners, selected filters, active modal forms, and temporary cached server responses).

> [!NOTE]
> **Data Reload & Restart Persistence**:
> - Any alumnus registration, batch coordinator assignment, RSVP submission, venue check-in, or memory upload persists across backend restarts, browser refreshes, and app reboots.

